 2. 🤖 AI boom drives record imports 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: U.S. Census Bureau ; Chart: Courtenay Brown/Axios U.S. imports hit a record $421 billion in August, Axios' Courtenay Brown reports from new government data. 

 Imports rose much faster than exports, widening the U.S. trade deficit by about 14% to $106 billion. (Still, the trade gap is about 20% smaller this year than at the same time last year.) 💻 Imports of semiconductors — critical to the data centers and computing infrastructure behind the AI buildout — jumped by a record $2.4 billion from July.

 Crude oil imports also rose sharply. The numbers underscore a tension at the heart of Trump's economic agenda: The administration wants to curb imports while accelerating an AI boom that heavily depends on them.

