 4. ✈️ 1 for the road: Aspen flight fight 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Illustration: Shoshana Gordon/Axios Planned upgrades to Aspen's airport sit at the core of a broader fight over the future of the iconic Colorado ski town, Andrew Zucker reports in The Wall Street Journal . 

 The plan calls for shifting the roughly 8,000-foot runway 80 feet to the west and widening it to 150 feet, to accommodate bigger jets used by some of the ultra-wealthy visitors who've become a staple of the Aspen crowd. 🛬 Proponents say that mountainous, hard-to-reach Aspen will benefit from easier access by air. 

 Detractors worry about being overrun with visitors — and the economic shock from closing the airfield for several months to do the work. Gift link . 

 
 
